ull-capacity temporary entry\n  array or a second packing pass.\n\nThe 2026-09-01 refactor also removed the legacy TP3/TilePalette kernels,\nGPU encoders, duplicate decode entry points, compatibility aliases, unused\ndecode metadata, and three research-only benchmark scripts. Native sources and\nthe extension are now named `chunk_delta3.*` / `chunk_delta3_ext`. KV codec\nsize and full-block capabilities live in the lightweight `kv_codec_spec.py`\nregistry, shared by tiered-serve and the vLLM planners without importing CUDA\ncompressor modules. Known codec allocation/copy/decode failures now fail fast;\nthe production KV decode path requires the published active-set plan and\n`cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` support.\n\nThe consolidated snapshot additionally contains:\n\n- host-native CD3 weight encoding with 64-row stripe parallelism;\n- adaptive OpenMP team sizing for a single KV compression worker;\n- batched NumPy KV slot allocation instead of a per-block Python loop;\n- production fused-MM crossover calibration through N=128 on GH200.\n- 128-thread standalone CD3 decode, with two logical chunks per thread;\n- two half-width live output accumulators with the same two 128-bit stores,\n  reducing standalone decode latency without changing the format;\n- 2-D `(tile, block)` KV decode launch geometry;\n- direct-to-cache indexed KV decode with no raw-BF16 intermediate copy;\n- selected-run KV staging for partial restores below the slot high-water mark.\n- one aligned slot-major CD3 blob and row-stride-aware CPU/GPU kernels;\n- one `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` submission for all K/V staging runs;\n- cached block/slot device metadata and one native K/V decode dispatch.\n- active-set identity/content caching with generation-safe invalidation;\n- a dense steady-state decode plan that skips filtering, sorting and run scans.\n- once-per-forward active-set publication instead of repeated per-layer NumPy\n  comparisons;\n- explicit-stream native paired decode dispatch;\n- a two-slot compressed-blob HBM ring that overlaps layer L+1 H2D with layer L\n  decode for N>=256, while preserving the cheaper one-stream path below it;\n- serving-suite codec selection through `--codecs p4flat,cd3`, including\n  codec-specific weight/KV arguments, configs, result labels and manifests;\n- a fully CPU P4Flat weight post-process (blocked relayout and subtile codec),\n  so CPU weight encoding no longer launches CUDA encode kernels;\n- a frozen-split weight benchmark that separately reports H2D, resident GPU\n  decode, and their combined latency.\n- projection-specific fused-N calibration overrides, with a uniform override\n  retained for compatibility;\n- exact-length CD3 frozen-split staging views, so standalone fallback accepts\n  variable-sized Packed20x3 exception streams;\n- startup route reporting that reflects projection-specific overrides.\n- a GH200/Llama-70B prefill weight-stream cutoff of N=1856: compressed\n  standalone decode below the cutoff and raw BF16 transfer at or above it;\n- an AST-level regression test that pins the calibrated CD3 cutoff.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The old CD3 patch's complete path set is contained in this patch.\n- Applied cleanly after startup prerequisites on source HEAD.\n- All 33 restored tiered-serve files matched the selected live files\n  byte-for-byte.\n- `git diff --check`, Python byte compilation, and shell syntax checks passed.\n- The consolidated patch applied after both startup prerequisites in a clean\n  worktree and all 32 restored files matched the live files byte-for-byte.\n- The vLLM integration patch reverse-checks against the validated live tree.\n- 33 CD3, prefill weight-stream, and KV-prefill policy tests passed.\n- The renamed `chunk_delta3_ext` built and imported successfully.\n- Synthetic CPU weight encode/GPU decode, CPU KV encode, and KV H2D+decode\n  smoke benchmarks were bit-exact.\n- Offline suite smoke (`cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp`, batch 1, input 8, output 2)\n  completed successfully and restored a clean GPU/